# Authoritative list of vendored Lua translation units compiled into the
# luaext extension. Consumers (config.m4, config.w32, tools/vendor-lua.sh)
# must ignore blank lines and lines whose first non-blank character is '#',
# and treat every remaining line as one file name relative to
# third_party/lua-5.5.1/src/.
#
# The upstream src/ tree is vendored complete and nothing is deleted from
# it, but these five translation units are deliberately NOT compiled:
#
#   lua.c      stand-alone interpreter front end (has a main())
#   luac.c     stand-alone bytecode compiler front end (has a main())
#   linit.c    upstream library opener; replaced by src/luaext_openlibs.c
#              so that no unwanted library is ever installed
#   liolib.c   real-filesystem io library; replaced by the VFS emulation
#   loadlib.c  package/require plus dlopen; replaced by luaext_require.c
#
# Leaving them out of the link is defence in depth: dlopen(), popen() and
# the real io library are then not merely unreachable from Lua, they are
# not in the binary at all.
#
# 29 files.
